# Gmail Unsubscriber - Environment Configuration
# 
# To use Gmail Unsubscriber, you need to set up OAuth 2.0 credentials in Google Cloud Console.
# 
# Steps to get your credentials:
# 1. Go to https://console.cloud.google.com
# 2. Create a new project or select an existing one
# 3. Enable the Gmail API:
#    - Click "Enable APIs and Services"
#    - Search for "Gmail API" and click "Enable"
# 4. Set up OAuth consent screen:
#    - Go to "APIs & Services" > "OAuth consent screen"
#    - Choose "External" user type
#    - Fill in required information (app name, user support email, etc.)
#    - Add scopes: gmail.readonly, gmail.modify, userinfo.email
#    - Save and continue
# 5. Create OAuth credentials:
#    - Go to "APIs & Services" > "Credentials"
#    - Click "Create Credentials" > "OAuth client ID"
#    - Choose "Desktop application"
#    - Click "Create"
#    - Copy the Client ID and Client Secret
# 6. Add your credentials below:

GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=your_client_id_here
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=your_client_secret_here

# IMPORTANT: Keep these credentials private!
# Do NOT commit this file to version control if it contains real credentials.
# Do NOT share these credentials with anyone.
